### --- Trigger log probe (discovery flow) --- ###

### Issue a probe code (block mode — default). Probe-bearing triggers are saved but NOT delivered to agents.
POST http://localhost:8180/control/manage/trigger-logs/probe
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "blockDelivery": true
}

> {%
  client.global.set("probeCode", response.body.response.code);
  client.global.set("probeIssuedAt", response.body.response.issuedAt);
%}

### Issue a probe code (pass mode — normal delivery, useful for diagnosing routing).
POST http://localhost:8180/control/manage/trigger-logs/probe
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "blockDelivery": false
}

### Simulate sending a trigger that contains the probe code (replace x-api-key with an active app key).
### Embed {{probeCode}} anywhere in the JSON payload.
POST http://localhost:8180/control/app/trigger/new
x-api-key: REPLACE_WITH_APP_KEY
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "trigger.message.new",
  "data": {
    "message": {
      "text": "probe {{probeCode}} hello"
    }
  }
}

### Poll for match (UI calls this every 1-2s). Returns matched=false until the trigger arrives.
GET http://localhost:8180/control/manage/trigger-logs/probe/match?code={{probeCode}}&since={{probeIssuedAt}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

### Invalid probe code format -> 400
GET http://localhost:8180/control/manage/trigger-logs/probe/match?code=garbage&since={{probeIssuedAt}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}
